How to apply the Adobe Commerce Cloud (ECE) patch for the Pearl Theme in an Ideal State environment
(static content deployed in the build phase)

Step 1:
Copy the content of this folder into the root of your Magento installation, merging the pub folder with yours.

Step 2:
If your stores use other Pearl based themes or other locales, open pearl_cloud_setups.sh and add them to the PearlThemes list, for example "Pearl/weltpixel_custom/de_DE". Do not use commas between the entries.

Step 3:
Add the script to the build hook of .magento.app.yaml, after the generate and transfer commands:

    build: |
        php ./vendor/bin/ece-tools build:generate
        php ./vendor/bin/ece-tools build:transfer
        chmod +x pearl_cloud_setups.sh
        ./pearl_cloud_setups.sh

Step 4:
Generate the Pearl LESS and CSS in the post_deploy hook, with one css:generate line for each store view that uses Pearl:

    post_deploy: |
        php ./vendor/bin/ece-tools post-deploy
        php ./bin/magento weltpixel:less:generate
        php ./bin/magento weltpixel:css:generate --store=default

Step 5:
Commit and push the changes.

Step 6:
After the first deploy, check on the server (for example after magento-cloud ssh) that each of the five module css folders is a symlink into pub/media/css_weltpixel:

    ls -ld app/code/WeltPixel/{CategoryPage,CustomHeader,CustomFooter,FrontendOptions,ProductPage}/view/frontend/web/css

Each line should end with "-> .../pub/media/css_weltpixel/<module>/css".

Then check the css folder of each theme and locale in PearlThemes the same way, one line per entry, for example:

    ls -ld pub/static/frontend/Pearl/weltpixel_custom/en_US/css

It should end with "-> .../pub/media/css_weltpixel/static/Pearl/weltpixel_custom/en_US/css".

If one of these is a normal folder, check that the script line is in the build hook, and look in the build log for "Pearl Cloud patch" errors or warnings.

Done!


Details about how this patch works:

In ECE environments app/code and the deployed static content are read-only once the application is deployed, so the LESS and CSS that Pearl generates from the theme options cannot be written there. The script replaces the folders Pearl writes to with symlinks into pub/media/css_weltpixel, which is a writable mount:
- the css folder of the modules that generate LESS (CategoryPage, CustomHeader, FrontendOptions, ProductPage, CustomFooter)
- the css folder of each theme and locale in PearlThemes, and the css folder of those modules in it

The files of those folders are placed in init/pub/media/css_weltpixel. build:transfer has already copied pub/media to init/pub/media at that point, and on every deploy ece-tools copies init/pub/media into the pub/media mount, so the files are where the symlinks point. Do not write files to pub/media in the build hook after build:transfer: the mount hides them.

The script works with and without a pub/static mount: with one it changes the static content that build:transfer moved to init/pub/static, without one the static content in pub/static.

The script stops with an error when a required folder is missing, and prints a warning for a module, theme or locale it cannot find.


Common questions:

Q: Do I need to run a script locally or commit files to pub/media?
A: No. The script runs in the build hook and creates everything it needs.

Q: The site shows the default Pearl styles right after a deploy.
A: Each deploy restores the CSS deployed in the build phase until the post_deploy hook regenerates it. Make sure the post_deploy commands from Step 4 are there for every store view.
